NAME
     sudo - run a command as another user, by policy

SYNOPSIS
     sudo [-u USER] [-i|-s] [COMMAND [ARG...]]
     sudo -l

DESCRIPTION
     sudo runs COMMAND as root, or as the user given by -u, if
     /etc/sudoers allows it. It asks for the *caller's* password, not
     the target's, and remembers the answer for a few minutes.

OPTIONS
     -u USER   run as USER rather than root
     -i        a login shell as that user
     -s        a shell as that user, keeping the environment
     -l        list what the caller may do

SEE ALSO
     su(1), /etc/sudoers, login(1)
